Saudi Arabia has no shortage of people who want to make games. Modern tools mean that even high school students in the Kingdom can now build a working platformer or get a 3D character moving around a scene. However, turning that into a company that survives realistic market conditions is a different matter entirely.&nbsp;

Closing that divide is what the Level Up Accelerator sets out to do: NEOM&rsquo;s 12-month programme supported by DigiPen Institute of Technology. It has now reached its third cohort and has funded 15 Saudi studios to date.&nbsp; ... [<a href="https://www.pocketgamer.biz/digipen-institutes-raymond-yan-a-gaming-hub-must-be-built-by-and-for-the-people-of-that-country/">MORE</a>]
